  "limits": [
    "A synthetic injection is a clean step; a real burn's transitional TLEs are not modelled, so recall is an upper bound for a real burn of the same size.",
    "Thinned series keep the ISS's per-TLE scatter, so thinned recall is optimistic for objects that are tracked less often and fitted from fewer observations.",
    "False-alarm rates are upper bounds: unannounced real burns count as detections.",
    "Wilson intervals treat trials as independent. Trials of different sizes can share a gap (distinct_injection_gaps per cadence), so intervals are somewhat optimistic where that count is small next to the trial count."
  ]
